  "details": "For well over two years, I've used VrChat on my AMD A10 APU with very usable framerates (around 20 fps in most worlds). Ever since Internal Debug Logic was introduced in Build ID: 19236179, and even after updating to Build ID: 19251301, now, in a black box world, even after lowering the resolution to the lowest possible setting of 640 x 480, I'm getting a barely navigable 9 fps. Both windowed and fullscreen modes were tested. All caches were flushed. All graphical settings have been set (and are always set) to their lowest (low or off when given the option). Any attempt at UI navigation (let alone game navigation) in a world that is more-developed than a black box is practically unrealistic. Processor: AMD A10-6800K APU with Radeon(tm) HD Graphics (4 CPUs), ~4.1GHz. Memory: 16384MB RAM. I run the title in Desktop mode on Windows 10. Game restarts and computer reboots did not solve the issue either. If you remove the Internal Debug Logic code, I could probably go back to using VrChat like I used to (and I am highly doubtful that I am the ONLY one impacted by this severe performance drop).",
